# Assessing the Humanities in the Primary School Using a Portfolio-Based Approach

**Authors:** Eaude, Tony

## Abstract
This article suggests that a portfolio-based approach to assessing the humanities in the primary school is appropriate and outlines what this might involve. It argues for a broad interpretation of &quot;the humanities&quot; and for adopting principles associated with formative assessment, where assessment is not equated with testing and a wide range of children's achievements are celebrated.

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ1152073

